# infant.cog
# A valid Ranvier program.
#
# Developmental modeling of an infant brain.
# Educational framing: Rita Carter et al., The Brain Book (DK, 2019),
# "The Infant Brain" / Development and Ageing.
#
# Physical bounds come from NIH 3D MRI-derived meshes (Nevit Dilmen):
#   3DPX-003765 whole brain, 3DPX-003145 FA white matter.
#
# Ranvier does not simulate a baby, score a baby, or compile a future.
# It only records what kind of information each name is allowed to be.

load atlas
load connectivity
load function
load behavior

# Persistent subject code — an ID may exist, but nothing else may become it.
ID subject_001

# Anatomy is REGION / STRUCTURE, never function or personality.
REGION frontal_lobe
REGION temporal_lobe
REGION parietal_lobe
REGION hippocampus
REGION cerebellum
REGION brainstem
STRUCTURE cerebrum

# White-matter pathways are TRACT.
TRACT arcuate_fasciculus
TRACT corpus_callosum

# Capabilities are NETWORK processes.
NETWORK sensory_network
NETWORK attention_network
NETWORK language_network
NETWORK memory_network
NETWORK default_mode_network

FUNCTION sensory_processing
FUNCTION attention
FUNCTION memory
FUNCTION language

# Development is temporary and measurable.
TEMP currently_learning
TEMP myelination_in_progress
PROCESS myelination
PROCESS synaptic_pruning
STATE current_alertness
STATE sleep_wake_cycle
PATTERN looking_preference
PREDICTION language_readiness

# Legal relations: function lives on a network, not on a lobe.
associate sensory_processing with sensory_network
associate attention with attention_network
associate memory with memory_network
associate language with language_network

connect frontal_lobe to temporal_lobe via arcuate_fasciculus

# Measurements stay measurements.
measure current_alertness of attention_network
measure currently_learning of sensory_network
measure myelination_in_progress of language_network

# Looking is observed behavior, not identity and not language itself.
observe infant_looking as looking_preference

# A future possibility may be estimated from a pattern.
# It remains a PREDICTION.
predict language_readiness from looking_preference

lookup frontal_lobe
lookup hippocampus["centroid"]
